        "managingDirector": "Sashidhar Jagdishan",
        "foundedYear": "1994",
        "businessSummary": "HDFC Bank believes that modern banking is about more than managing money; it's about fulfilling aspirations and shaping the futures of its customers and communities. The institution's core purpose is to help every Indian make better money choices, for both today and for the future, fostering financial well-being nationwide. A key principle for the bank is 'Digital First, Customer Always,' focusing on making banking seamless, intuitive, and personal in an era of digital disruption. It serves customers at every stage of their financial journey, whether they are in major cities, semi-urban towns, or rural heartlands. Following its successful merger with HDFC Limited, the bank has become a stronger financial services entity, enhancing its ability to provide end-to-end financial solutions. With 9,455 strategically located branches, 51% of which are in semi-urban and rural areas, it broadens access for previously underserved markets.",
