        "foundedYear": "1973",
        "businessSummary": "Coal India Limited (CIL) is India's largest coal producer, operating under the Ministry of Coal and celebrating five decades of ensuring the nation's energy security and progress. Its vision is to emerge as a global player in the primary energy sector, committed to providing energy security through environmentally and socially sustainable growth using best practices. The company's mission is to produce and market planned quantities of coal and its products efficiently and economically in an eco-friendly way, with attention to safety and quality. For business sustainability, the company is diversifying into new revenue streams such as critical minerals, renewable energy, coal gasification, pump storage systems, and thermal power. The company operates through ten wholly-owned Indian subsidiaries, managing 310 mines across eight states in India, featuring opencast, underground, and mixed mining formats. In fiscal year 2024-25, CIL achieved its highest-ever production volume of approximately 781.06 million tonnes, a record-breaking performance for the company.",
