    "profile": {
      "overview": "Lamosaic India Ltd trades and supplies decorative laminates, acrylic sheets, plywood, and interior architectural decorative surface panels.",
      "productsAndServices": "Lamosaic India Ltd operates in Miscellaneous (Founded 2020).",
      "businessModel": "SME issue (EQUITY) listed on NSE / BSE · ISIN INE0R0201012.",
      "industryOverview": "Miscellaneous primary market offering tracked via SEBI & exchange filings.",
      "competitivePosition": "Consolidated subscription recorded at 1.55x.",
      "promoters": [
        "Mr. Vinod Juthalal Visaria"
      ],
      "growthOpportunities": [],
      "strengths": [
        "Lamosaic India claims to adapt quickly to fluctuating market trends by continually introducing new and innovative designs and products. ",
        "Lamosaic India leverages word-of-mouth marketing, advertising, and promoting its products. The company actively distributes its design offerings directly to a network that includes dealers, distributors, stockists, and wholesalers.",
        "The company has seen a consistent increase in revenue from operations and profit after tax (PAT) over the past few years. Revenue from operations increased from Rs 10.01 crore in FY22 to Rs 31.67 crore in FY23 to Rs 55.64 crore in FY24, while PAT increased from Rs 0.51 crore in FY22 to Rs 4.07 crore in FY23 to Rs 8.23 crore in FY24."
      ],
      "risks": [
        "Lamosaic India has a relatively brief operating history. The company has been in operation only for 4 years; therefore, predicting its future potential since its recent transition to a public limited company based on its past performance could be a challenge for investors.",
        "The company's operations are confined geographically to Maharashtra. Any adverse developments in the business environment of the region could negatively impact the company’s operations. ",
        "A significant portion of Lamosaic India's revenue comes from its laminates product line. Laminates contributed 86%, 83.92%, 81.99%, and 93.34% in the six months ended on September 30, 2024, FY24, FY23, and FY22, respectively, to the revenue from operations. Any adverse developments in this segment or a decrease in demand for them could hurt the company’s business. ",
        "The company's manufacturing capabilities hinge on a single workshop located in Chembur, Maharashtra. Any disruption in this unit could hurt Lamosaic India's operations and financial stability.",
        "As of September 20, 2024, Lamosaic India had a total outstanding debt (secured and unsecured borrowings) of Rs 14.76 crore. Any inability to repay or service these loans could adversely affect the company’s financial position. ",
        "There are ongoing legal proceedings involving Lamosaic India's promoters and associated entities. Any adverse judgments in any of these cases could be detrimental to the company’s business prospects.",
        "The company has witnessed negative cash flows in the past. Any repeat of that in the future, would be negative for the company’s business."
      ]
    },
